https://api.github.com/users/mwichro","html_url":"https://github.com/mwichro","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":11,"created_at":"2026-06-16T10:42:51Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T09:12:15Z","closed_at":"2026-07-02T09:12:15Z","assignee":{"login":"mwichro","id":32612987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNjEyOTg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32612987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro","html_url":"https://github.com/mwichro","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mwichro/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the bug\n\nI've been hitting a `CUDA_ERROR_ILLEGAL_ADDRESS` on H100 when running some complex XLA GEMM fusions.\n\nAfter digging into the IR, this is a regression from PR #10234. That PR relaxed the check in `Utility.cpp` from `% 16 == 0` to `% 8 == 0` to allow `wgmma` to handle `N=8` TF32 tiles. \n\nThe problem is that while the PTX ISA does support `N=8`, it requires the shared memory to be padded properly. @ThomasRaoux actually pointed this out in an older PR (#7981) when he originally added the `% 16` check:\n> *\"This prevent generating miscompiles for cases where the N dimension is too small. Technically we could support N=8 but it would require padding the shared memory.\"*\n\nBecause the SMEM allocator isn't padding these `N=8` tensors to 16 elements, the WGMMA descriptor reads out of bounds and therefore the illegal address. I guess the reason the unit tests (like `test_dot_wgmma_tf32_n8k8`) didn't catch this is because they use very little shared memory, so the out-of-bounds read just harmlessly fetches zeros. But in PyTorch Inductor where multiple tensors are tightly packed in SMEM, the read either fetches garbage or hits the physical SMEM limit and crashes the GPU.\n\nTo verify, I manually reverted `retShapePerCTA[rank - 1] % 8 == 0` back to `% 16 == 0` for `version == 3` locally. This correctly forced the kernel to fall back to MMAv2 (`mma.sync`), and the exact same Inductor workload passed flawlessly.\n\nShould we revert the `version == 3` checks in `Utility.cpp` back to `% 16` until the layout engine supports SMEM padding for `N=8`? Happy to open a quick PR if that's the preferred route!\n\nPS: I really tried to write a minimal Python reproducer for this, but I couldn't get it to crash reliably. I suspect it's because you need the SMEM allocator to pack the tensor right at the edge of the memory limit to actually trigger the illegal address fault, which my simple test wasn't doing (but Inductor's heavy kernels do).\n\n### Environment details\n\n- **Triton version:** originally `3de9d04738` ( from PR #10234) but could be reproduced in `main`.\n- H100 (sm 90)\n","closed_by":{"login":"karupayun","id":8610429,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2MTA0Mjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8610429?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/karupayun","html_url":"https://github.com/karupayun","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karupayun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karupayun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karupayun/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karupayun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karupayun/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karupayun/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karupayun/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karupayun/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karupayun/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/10629/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/10629/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}